; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Josephus Circle
; CATEGORY: Puzzles & Logic
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     lists, circles, counting, animation
; SUMMARY:  People stand in a circle and every third one steps out; where should you stand to be the last?
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Twelve numbered players stand in a ring. Counting round the ring,
;   every third player steps out and turns grey, and the counting
;   carries on from the next player. The last one left wins. The
;   puzzle is named after Flavius Josephus, the historian, who told
;   a story about such a circle. Can you guess the winner before the
;   turtle finishes?
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. Change the numbers in the last line, for
;   example "josephus 10 2", for a different size of ring or count.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a list used as a ring: move the front player to the back
;   * placing things evenly around a circle with the turtle
;   * BUTFIRST to remove the player who steps out
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * With a count of 2, try rings of 1 to 16 players and write down
;     the winners. Do you see the pattern?
;   * Collect the players who step out in a list and print it at the end.
; ============================================================

; Go to the place in the ring where player p stands.
to gospot :p
  penup home
  right 360 * (:p - 1) / :size
  forward 200
end

; Draw a player as a colored disc with its number on it.
to player :p :color
  gospot :p
  setpencolor :color setpensize 50
  dot pos
  setheading 0 back 6 left 90 forward 5 + 4 * int :p / 10 right 90
  setpencolor 7 label :p
end

; Move the first player in the ring to the back.
to rotate :ring
  output lput first :ring butfirst :ring
end

to josephus :size :count
  clearscreen hideturtle
  setbackground [245 240 230]
  setlabelheight 18
  for [p 1 :size] [player :p [50 110 200]]
  localmake "ring iseq 1 :size
  while [(count :ring) > 1] [
    ; skip past count - 1 players, then the next one is out
    repeat :count - 1 [make "ring rotate :ring]
    wait 30
    player first :ring [180 180 180]
    print (sentence [Player] first :ring [steps out.])
    make "ring butfirst :ring
  ]
  player first :ring [230 160 30]
  penup home setheading 0 back 10 left 90 forward 60 right 90
  setpencolor 0 label (sentence [Player] first :ring [wins!])
  print (sentence [The winner is player] first :ring)
end

josephus 12 3
